# Cloud Build source-upload filter.
#
# `gcloud builds submit` uses THIS file instead of `.gitignore` when it exists,
# so every protection `.gitignore` provided is repeated here — dropping one would
# upload something it was hiding.
#
# Why it exists: the build had been uploading ~1.9 GiB per run, almost all of it
# untracked video assets under `packages/reactor-video/`. Everything below is
# either regenerated during the build, not needed by it, or must not leave the
# machine.

# --- must never be uploaded ---------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.env.local
**/.env.production.local
**/.env.preview.local
.custody
**/custody-audit.jsonl
*.pem
*.key
*.p8

# --- regenerated by the build -------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/coverage
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- not needed to build the image -------------------------------------------
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, deliberately. An unanchored `data` matches ANY
# directory named `data` at any depth — including `packages/ux-workflow/src/data/`
# — which broke the build twice before this was caught.
/data
/docs
/archive
/.vercel
/.agents
/.claude
/.commandcode
/.impeccable
/--full-page
/packages/reactor-video
/skills-lock.json

# --- large media (the bulk of the old upload) ---------------------------------
# Scoped to video only, and only where it actually lives (the heavy directories
# are already excluded above). Deliberately NOT a global `**/*.png`: image assets
# can be legitimately imported by a package's source, and silently dropping them
# would be a confusing build failure.
**/*.mov
**/*.mp4
**/*.webm

# --- noise --------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore
.dockerignore
**/.DS_Store
*.log
